0 FILE triceratops.ldr
0 BRICK Triceratops 77985 reconstruction draft
0 Name: triceratops-v0.mpd
0 Evidence printed pages 148–149 / steps 278–279: two-pin link is assembled internally, then docked to the anterior torso. Provisional port roles: 32184 crosshole toward skull; remaining 32140 hole toward torso. Exact mating identities remain unverified.
0 The step-278 link is a local submodel. Step279 docks its remaining 32140 hole provisionally to the torso; the orthogonal 32184 port is provisionally skull-side. Step247/249 receiver identities and engagement remain uncertain. Independent base steps 280–288 are modeled locally with unverified outer-panel contacts.
0 Author: BRICK project
0 !BRICK_STATE {"schema_version":3,"status":"instruction_reconstruction_in_progress","model":"Triceratops fossil reconstruction","reference_set":"LEGO 77985","reference_url":"https://www.lego.com/cdn/product-assets/product.bi.core.pdf/6649862.pdf","manual_files":["6649862-1.pdf","6649862-2.pdf"],"progress_note":"Steps 247–249 torso candidates and the step278 link remain local. Step278 has two internal 11214 pins; based on the 278→279 sequence 32184 is provisionally skull-side and the remaining 32140 port torso-side, so torso alignment does not require both orthogonal ports. User retained 6577/43093 and parallel/orthogonal alternatives as uncertain; no repeat question. Independent base steps 280–288 are represented; step289 local branch includes the visible plate/hook/round-cap sequence; step290 opposite-side plate branch has begun, with exact shape and stack candidates provisional, with step288 wedge contacts provisional, with step284 3021/3022 identities supported by the callout and placements provisional. Steps291–292 were checked: they articulate existing panel assemblies and add no physical pieces. The pivot/pose transforms remain unresolved. piece_count is MPD instance-record count only, not confirmed instruction quantity; mutually exclusive alternatives are not simultaneously instantiated. Steps291–292 articulation and step293 flank context are recorded; their exact hinge/contact transforms remain local and provisional. Step294 plaque/minifigure are excluded. No additional physical placements are counted for these annotation-only steps. Step250 is now represented by one 3710 shape-matched local plate fragment; its final body stud row and transform remain provisional. Step251 now has four candidate placements from the callout count/shape; body contacts and orientation remain provisional and are not confirmed quantities. Step252 now includes one 50950 curved-slope shape candidate registered over the 11458 row; exact mold and insertion remain provisional. Steps253–254 are now represented as two local plate/round-plate pairs. Internal two-stud geometry is registered; exact round mold and torso-side transforms remain provisional. Steps291–292 hinge tracking now includes the 50340 candidate DAT axis in each local branch; panel mating and fold angles remain unresolved. Steps256–258 now have five local placements for the visible L-shaped rib fragment; the unidentified step255 joint is isolated as the only omitted dependency, and no body transform is asserted. Step259 now includes a local 6541/2736 candidate connection with calculated shaft span, plus provisional 32000/54200 upper parts; unresolved round spacers are held out rather than counted as completed pieces.","piece_count":103,"unique_sale_skus":7,"listed_retail_parts_cost_cny":"0.95","cost_scope":"Not totaled; candidate mappings only.","target_dimensions_cm":{"length":null,"height":null,"width":null},"reference_geometry_bounds_cm":{"length":null,"height":null,"width":null},"support_count":0,"support_verification":"Not assessed.","validation":{"instruction_scope":"printed page 136 step247; page137 step249; page142 step263; printed pages 143–149 steps264–279: body mount and skull docking callouts inspected; printed p150 steps280–281: separate base strip started; printed p151 step282: tile cover added; printed p151 step283: 1x2 plate, Technic brick, and dual-finger hinge candidates placed; printed p151 step284: one 2x3 plate and one 2x2 plate added to independent base; printed p151 step285: two double-curved slope shape candidates placed; printed p152 step286 and p153 side views: paired large triangular panels registered as 30355/30356 shape candidates; printed p154 step287: left/right curved perforated panels identified as 67142/68196 shape candidates; printed p154 step288: two small handed wedge candidates per outer side registered; printed p155 step289 substeps 1–2: local 3666/3020 plate pair registered; printed p155 step289 substeps 3–5: modified hinge, rounded-end bar/plate and round cap shape candidates placed; printed p156 step290: opposite-side local plate/hook branch started; printed p157 steps291–292: fold arrows checked; articulation adds no parts, exact pivot mapping/fold transforms unresolved; printed p158 step293 final-view panel context inspected (flank location visible, mating axes hidden); printed p159 step294 plaque/minifigure callout excluded per user scope; printed p137 step250: one tan 1x4 plate shape-identified as official 3710 by four-stud count, placed in independent local fragment; printed p137 step251: three offset-peghole plate shapes and one small wedge candidate recorded as an independent local callout assembly; printed p138 step252: one long curved tan slope candidate placed over the provisional step251 row; printed p138 steps253–254: two local 3023b/4032a pairs registered to the two-stud drop arrows; 4032a remains shape candidate; printed p139 steps256–258: two 3710 plates, two 3023b plate candidates and one 54200 wedge candidate registered in a local L-shaped fragment; step255 corner connector withheld; printed p140 step259: local 6541/2736 side-hole fit and 32000/54200 upper candidates recorded; 6577/2780 spacer alternatives remain uninstantiated","placements":"Step278 internal two-pin fit: official DAT centerlines have 0 LDU transverse residual and 20 LDU face spacing; the nominal 11214 pin sections span their 32140/32184 bores. Step247 6541 hole center [20,20,20], axis +Y, is coaxial with the free 32140 port and its adjoining face; the two 6577 candidates are stacked vertically below the 6541, not placed through the side hole. Step249 support holes are 20 LDU apart and their candidate 43093/62462 axes are aligned; actual pin depth and whether the second 6541 axis is parallel or orthogonal remain unresolved; the user retained both candidates. 32184 is provisionally skull-side and the remaining 32140 port torso-side, so the receiver is not required to align with both axes. Step279 has no parts in its callout; the required sockets must pre-exist on the body. Step280 base strip uses a 2x10 plate with a 50340 dual-finger hinge candidate across its end; step281 has paired 1x3 plates on adjacent rows. These are independent local coordinates and remain diagram-based pending later platform stages. Official candidate port calculations: step249 6541 axes are both +Z and 20 LDU apart; each 43093 and the near hole of each 62462 are coaxial. The currently modeled far sockets are [390,-14,50] and [410,-14,50], both +Z. Step278 link has two remaining external candidates with +Y and +Z axes; the step278 ports now have separate provisional roles: 32184 toward the skull and the remaining 32140 hole toward the torso, following step279 docking order. Therefore the torso receiver need not fit both orthogonal axes. Keep the step249 parallel/orthogonal axis question local and unresolved; do not reject its candidate from a two-port mismatch alone. Step282 tile 2x4 is placed over the hinge-end studs as a diagram-based provisional cover. Step283 candidate rows use two official DAT height registrations: 3023b row at 8 LDU, 3700 row at 24 LDU, with 50340 plates stacked at the corresponding top levels. Finger direction and exact rows remain provisional. Step284 adds one 3021 2x3 plate and one 3022 2x2 plate to the independent base; IDs and official DAT shapes are registered, while exact overlap/row remain provisional. Step285 adds two 1762 double-curved slope shape candidates based on callout curvature and count; exact ID/orientation and stud footprint remain unverified. Step286 places one 30355/30356 mirrored 6x12-wing shape candidate on either side of the base; footprint and scale follow the manual, but mold allocation, hinge contact and engagement height remain tentative. Step287 adds one 67142/68196 left/right panel candidate based on four-hole pattern and tapered silhouette. Local long-axis alignment and edge offset are provisional; pin-axis engagement/depth not yet resolved. Step288 places two 24299 left-shape and two 24307 right-shape candidates, following the separate official left/right mold forms and 2x callouts; exact face, orientation and contact with the perforated panels remain provisional. Step289 independent branch begins with a 3666 1x6 plate and 3020 2x4 plate. Four stud centers align at 20-LDU pitch and vertical layer uses an 8-LDU plate offset; final attachment to the platform is withheld. Step289 substeps 3–5 continue the local independent branch with a 3023b plate, 50340 hinge candidate, 77850 rounded-end 1x3 candidate and 4032a round 2x2 candidate. Their local stack direction is diagram-based provisional; no external connection is asserted. Step290 begins a separate opposing-side assembly with a 3666/3020 plate pair and the 3023b/50340/77850/4032a support stack as shape candidates. Its 67142/68196 panel attachments are not placed until their branch contact is visible from later callouts. Steps291–292 add no physical instances: manual arrows show articulation of existing side panels, but exact pivot datums and target angles are unresolved; no candidate parts or alternate poses are counted as added inventory. Step293 shows the side-panel assembly on the fossil flank, but no mating point or axis; triceratops-base-289/290 remain independent local subassemblies pending connector evidence. Step294 plaque/minifigure are excluded and add no instances. Step250 adds one 3710 plate in a local fragment, long axis along the depicted body beam. The actual stud row, overlap and torso transform are unverified. Step251 adds three 11458 shape candidates and one 54200 slope candidate to a separate local fragment. Their shared placement is a callout layout only; exact contact, facing and torso transform remain unverified. Step252 50950 candidate rotated 90 degrees over the three 11458 candidates; 60x20 LDU footprint spans their 20-LDU pitch with nominal zero footprint residual. This is shape/pitch registration, not mold identification or insertion validation. Steps253–254: each 3023b pair is modeled beneath a 4032a round-plate candidate. 3023b stud centers at x=±10, z=10 align with a row of 4032a underside sockets at 20-LDU pitch; round plate bottom face is at y=0 after an 8-LDU offset. The central axlehole passes along local Y and remains unused/open. These are local fits only; the body attachment transform is deferred. Step289/290 50340 candidate DAT hinge axes were checked: each current identity transform preserves local +Z and the part-defined centerline y=2, finger-center span z=-16..+16 (32 LDU). Steps291–292 confirm panel articulation qualitatively, but do not identify the mating knuckles, pivot co-location, engagement depth or final angle; no transform was invented. Step252 vertical check: official 50950 bottom datum y=24 at instance y=-24 reaches y=0, matching the 11458 top datum y=0 for nominal 0-LDU face gap. This does not verify stud/recess engagement depth. Official 4032a comparison uses the central axlehol3/axlehol2 geometry, four peripheral studs and 8-LDU plate body. 18674 has a center stud instead of an open center hole; 30000 is a 2x2 brick with side pins and 24-LDU body. Both are worse fits to the enlarged callout, but no printed mold ID is visible. Steps256–258 are represented as a local two-arm L fragment. The 1x4 plate count/footprints are called out; the right-angle arrangement is diagram-based. Step257/258 plate reinforcement positions and 54200 facing are provisional. The 255 joint that ties the arms and the final body transform remain unresolved. Official 54200 bottom datum y=0 is positioned at y=8 to meet the 3023b top datum y=8 in step258; this height contact is provisional because the part identity/facing is candidate-level. Step259 2736 candidate axle axis is local X and is rotated onto 6541 +Z hole in -Z direction. The official 17.5-LDU shaft enters the 20-LDU hole 17.5 LDU, leaving 2.5 LDU to the far face; the ball center remains 12 LDU outside the near face. This is a geometry-fit candidate, not printed ID confirmation. 32000 and 54200 remain provisional upper placements; unclear round spacers are not double-counted.","catalog_and_asset_references":"official LDraw parts 32140, 32184, 98989, 11214 inspected; GoBricks SKU mappings remain unverified","full_connection_graph":"Step278 11214 pair is consumed internally between 32184 and the two connected 32140 holes. The remaining 32140 hole is the provisional torso-side port because step279 docks the completed link to the anterior torso; the 32184 orthogonal crosshole is the provisional skull-side port. These port-role assignments follow assembly order but remain subject to exact contact-part confirmation. A torso receiver is not required to satisfy both axes. The 247 single-hole candidate has 0 LDU transverse axis residual and 0 LDU face gap to the 32140 port; this is coordinate registration only. Step249’s paired support remains a candidate and its connection role/transform is unresolved. Printed p158 step293 supports only the qualitative flank association of the 289–292 panels; the hidden interface does not establish a connector, axis, insertion length or numeric assembly transform. Printed p159 step294 plaque and minifigure remain outside scope. Side-panel fold candidate: the official 50340 DAT carries a +Z hinge axis with fingers at z=±16. In the current independent 289/290 fragments each hinge candidate retains local +Z. The 291–292 arrows establish movement, not the exact mating part or angle.","exact_mesh_collision":"unverified_open_surface_probe_ambiguous","physical_build":"not_tested","mesh_collision_note":"A Blender Boolean probe was attempted after recursively triangulating LDraw DAT references. The flattened 32140 mesh retained 148 non-manifold edges of 2762; 32184 retained 360/2170; 11214 retained 383/1378; 6541 retained 56/520. Intersection volumes were nonzero small artifacts even for intended face contacts, so these booleans cannot establish collision-free fit. Use only the independently computed hole-axis/face-spacing checks until watertight solid reconstruction is available. The later step249 candidate probe likewise showed intersecting triangles at intended pin/receiver, joiner/pin and plate/brick interfaces; no valid solid-overlap result was produced.","surface_collision_note":"Open-triangle BVH tests were run on unmodified official LDraw meshes after the initial 278 link and again on the step249 candidate support. The 249 test reported intersections/zero nearest-surface distance at 6541↔43093, 43093↔62462, plate↔brick, and adjacent brick contacts. This watertightness-independent surface check cannot distinguish intended contact/friction engagement from penetration and cannot test containment. Result is ambiguous/unverified, not a collision-free pass. Keep separate from closed-solid Boolean probes, which were invalidated by non-manifold input.","open_questions":[{"id":"step247-small-round-parts","status":"deferred_user_uncertain_keep_candidates","manual_page":136,"step":247,"candidates":["6577.dat Technic Bush 1/2 Type 2","43093.dat Technic Axle Pin with Friction"],"evidence":"P136 exploded callout shows two small ring-like parts in a vertical stack below a 6541 candidate. 6577 has a female axle bore and fits the ring silhouette but requires an underlying shaft; 43093 has a male friction-pin form that can enter the 6541 side hole but is inconsistent with the depicted vertical spacer placement. Full product inventory thumbnails on printed pages 161–162 were checked against the two-item callout and surrounding assembly. The inventory prints LEGO element numbers rather than LDraw mold numbers; its small round connector thumbnails do not distinguish the concealed female axle bore from a protruding male pin at this view, so it narrows quantity/appearance but does not resolve 6577 vs 43093.","needed":"Already answered unclear/retain candidates. Do not ask again; revisit only if later assembly views expose the end profile or an independently verified element-to-mold mapping."},{"id":"step249-receiver-axis","status":"deferred_user_uncertain_keep_candidates","manual_page":137,"step":249,"candidates":["parallel 6541 hole axes","orthogonal 6541 hole axes"],"evidence":"The user asked to retain both orientations while uncertain. 32184 is provisionally skull-side and the remaining 32140 port torso-side, so the torso receiver need not align to both link axes. Parallel/orthogonal comparison alone does not eliminate either receiver candidate. The complete inventory thumbnail pages (printed 161–162) and page137 step249 callout were cross-checked; element-number-only inventory plus the obscured rear face does not establish the second 6541 axis. Port-role evidence from steps278–279 means this axis comparison cannot alone exclude a receiver candidate.","needed":"Already answered unclear/retain candidates. Do not ask again; use a later reverse-side or direct mating view if it appears."}]},"nodes":{"skull-torso-link":{"origin":"midpoint between the two registered 32140 beam-hole centers; local +Y is their shared axis; local Z separation is 40 LDU","root_transform_status":"local subassembly only; global transform withheld until skull and torso mating datums are measured","remaining_32140_hole_candidate":{"center":[20,0,20],"axis":[0,1,0],"candidate_receiver":"6541.dat","receiver_hole_center":[20,20,20],"receiver_axis":[0,1,0],"transverse_residual_ldu":0,"face_gap_ldu":0,"status":"diagram_based_tentative; assigned as the single torso-side port candidate from the step278→279 assembly sequence; exact receiver, part identity and insertion depth remain unconfirmed"},"link_ports":{"beam_free_hole_candidate":{"part":"32140.dat","center":[20,0,20],"axis":[0,1,0],"role":"provisional torso-side port: step279 docks this completed link to the anterior torso; this is the remaining 32140 hole, subject to exact receiver confirmation"},"crossblock_crosshole_candidate":{"part":"32184.dat","center":[0,20,0],"axis":[0,0,1],"role":"provisional skull-side port: 32184 is the compact cross block on the skull-side end of the step278 link; mating skull part/pin remains unverified"},"bridge_pins":{"part":"11214.dat","count":2,"centerline_z":[-20,20],"axis":[0,1,0],"role":"official-DAT-fit axle sections seat 20 LDU into 32184; pin sections traverse 32140; they join the two link pieces, not yet assigned to an external endpoint"}},"two_port_test":{"step278_roles":"32184 orthogonal crosshole is the provisional skull-side port; 32140 remaining hole is the provisional torso-side port, based on link topology and step279 docking sequence.","geometry":"The body-side receiver need only align to the 32140 port if the 32184 end belongs to the skull. Do not reject a torso receiver based on requiring it to match both +Y and +Z ports.","step249_parallel_candidate":{"centers":[[390,-14,50],[410,-14,50]],"axes":[[0,0,1],[0,0,1]],"pitch_ldu":20,"status":"retain as a candidate body support; its two outlets are not both required to mate to the torso if only the 32140 port is body-side. Exact port correspondence, transform and insertion remain unresolved."},"step247_single_port_candidate":{"link_center":[20,0,20],"link_axis":[0,1,0],"receiver_center":[20,20,20],"receiver_axis":[0,1,0],"transverse_residual_ldu":0,"face_gap_ldu":0,"status":"coordinate/axis registration only; receiver identity and mechanical engagement are not confirmed"}}},"independent-base-280":{"origin":"local datum at center of 2x10 plate, isolated at world X=600 to keep it independent from torso/skull fragments","parts":[{"id":"part-0052","part":"3832.dat","role":"2x10 tan base plate; shape/stud count confirmed"},{"id":"part-0053","part":"50340.dat","role":"1x2 dual-finger hinge shape candidate; direction provisional"},{"id":"part-0054","part":"3623.dat","role":"first 1x3 plate, adjacent base row; placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0055","part":"3623.dat","role":"second 1x3 plate, adjacent base row; placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0056","part":"87079.dat","role":"step282 2x4 tile cover candidate; placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0057","part":"3023b.dat","role":"step283 1x2 plate row; position provisional"},{"id":"part-0058","part":"3700.dat","role":"step283 1x2 Technic brick with two holes; row/orientation provisional"},{"id":"part-0059","part":"50340.dat","role":"step283 first dual-finger hinge candidate; direction provisional"},{"id":"part-0060","part":"50340.dat","role":"step283 second dual-finger hinge candidate; direction provisional"},{"id":"part-0061","part":"3021.dat","role":"step284 2x3 plate; identity supported by six-stud callout and official shape, placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0062","part":"3022.dat","role":"step284 2x2 plate; identity supported by four-stud callout/underside and official shape, placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0063","part":"1762.dat","role":"step285 first of two 2x2 double-curved slope candidates; shape/quantity candidate, transform provisional"},{"id":"part-0064","part":"1762.dat","role":"step285 second double-curved slope candidate; paired row provisional"},{"id":"part-0065","part":"30355.dat","role":"step286 large studded triangular wing panel; official 6x12 left shape candidate, side/hinge transform provisional"},{"id":"part-0066","part":"30356.dat","role":"step286 mirrored 6x12 right wing panel candidate; exact callout mold allocation and hinge transform provisional"},{"id":"part-0067","part":"67142.dat","role":"step287 left 5x13 curved perforated panel candidate; outer edge registration provisional"},{"id":"part-0068","part":"68196.dat","role":"step287 right 5x13 curved perforated panel candidate; mirrored fit and hole engagement provisional"},{"id":"part-0069","part":"24299.dat","role":"step288 one of the counted pair on corresponding side; official handed wing shape candidate, precise contact provisional"},{"id":"part-0070","part":"24299.dat","role":"step288 one of the counted pair on corresponding side; official handed wing shape candidate, precise contact provisional"},{"id":"part-0071","part":"24307.dat","role":"step288 one of the counted pair on corresponding side; official handed wing shape candidate, precise contact provisional"},{"id":"part-0072","part":"24307.dat","role":"step288 one of the counted pair on corresponding side; official handed wing shape candidate, precise contact provisional"}],"status":"independent subassembly draft; steps 280–288 represented; outer wedge positions remain provisional"},"base-extension-289-local":{"origin":"center datum of the brown 3666 1x6 plate; independent step289 plate pair, held at world X=900 until its attachment point on the main base is measured","parts":[{"id":"part-0073","part":"3666.dat","role":"step289 brown 1x6 base; six-stud row confirmed by callout"},{"id":"part-0074","part":"3020.dat","role":"step289 tan 2x4 cap; four studs align to one row of 3666, row offset provisional"},{"id":"part-0075","part":"3023b.dat","role":"Printed p155 step289 callout: tan 1x2 plate by two-stud count. Placed at the free end of the local 3666/3020 pair; row/overlap provisional."},{"id":"part-0076","part":"50340.dat","role":"Printed p155 step289 callout: 1x2 modified hinge plate candidate. Local branch placement follows the successive substep, but finger direction and connection surface are provisional. Official DAT axis candidate +Z at y=2; step291–292 movement supports articulation but exact engagement/fold angle is unresolved."},{"id":"part-0077","part":"77850.dat","role":"Printed p155 step289: rounded-end reddish-brown 1x3 plate candidate, based on three-stud icon. Placed above the hinge area; exact part identity and row are provisional."},{"id":"part-0078","part":"4032a.dat","role":"Printed p155 step289 final callout: round tan 2x2 plate candidate, aligned above the brown round-end element. Center-hole identity and exact vertical layer remain unverified."}],"status":"steps289 substeps 1–5 represented locally; panel-to-base contact and final platform transform unverified","hinge_axis_check":{"part_candidate":"50340.dat","local_axis":[0,0,1],"local_axis_line_point":[0,2,0],"finger_centers_z":[-16,16],"current_instance_rotation":"identity; local +Z preserved","manual_evidence":"steps291–292 show adjacent panels rotating about the hinge row","status":"axis candidate registered; mating half/knuckles, pivot co-location, insertion and final angle unverified"}},"base-extension-290-local":{"origin":"center of brown 3666 1x6 local plate; separate branch on the opposing platform side, world X=1200 only as isolation placement","parts":[{"id":"part-0079","part":"3666.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290: six-stud reddish-brown 1x6 plate, local datum for opposite extension branch."},{"id":"part-0080","part":"3020.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290: eight-stud tan 2x4 plate aligned to one 3666 stud row; exact row offset diagram-based."},{"id":"part-0081","part":"3023b.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290: tan 1x2 plate candidate at the branch tip; local attachment row provisional."},{"id":"part-0082","part":"50340.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290 modified hinge plate shape candidate; finger direction and contact surface provisional. Official DAT axis candidate +Z at y=2; step291–292 movement supports articulation but exact engagement/fold angle is unresolved."},{"id":"part-0083","part":"77850.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290 three-stud rounded-end reddish-brown plate candidate, placed in the illustrated hinge stack provisionally."},{"id":"part-0084","part":"4032a.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290 round 2x2 plate/cap candidate on the local hinge stack; bore identity and depth unresolved."}],"status":"partial local subassembly; step290 perforated left/right panels are held only at their unresolved branch contacts while the plate/hook base proceeds","hinge_axis_check":{"part_candidate":"50340.dat","local_axis":[0,0,1],"local_axis_line_point":[0,2,0],"finger_centers_z":[-16,16],"current_instance_rotation":"identity; local +Z preserved","manual_evidence":"steps291–292 show adjacent panels rotating about the hinge row","status":"axis candidate registered; mating half/knuckles, pivot co-location, insertion and final angle unverified"}},"torso-extension-250-local":{"origin":"center of official 3710 plate; long axis local X, kept independent from body receiver until the stud row is visible","root_transform_status":"diagram-matched local extension; root X=1600 is only an isolation coordinate; body contact transform unresolved"},"torso-detail-251-local":{"origin":"center of the small step251 callout grouping, isolated from the torso and step250 fragment","root_transform_status":"callout silhouette/count placed locally; part facing, pin/peghole assignment and body transform remain provisional pending step252/253 and opposite-side views","step252":{"part":"50950.dat","position":[0,-24,10],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"evidence":"3x1 footprint and 11458 20-LDU stud pitch align after a quarter turn","status":"shape registration provisional; mold identity/insertion unverified","vertical_datum":{"50950_dat_bottom_y":24,"instance_y":-24,"resulting_bottom_y":0,"11458_top_datum_y":0,"nominal_face_gap_ldu":0,"status":"height registration checked; stud/recess engagement depth and mold identity unverified"}}},"torso-side-253-local":{"origin":"center axis of the 4032a 2x2 round plate; local +Y is the through axlehole axis","root_transform_status":"confirmed internal stud-pitch registration to 3023b; external torso-side placement and facing unresolved"},"torso-side-254-local":{"origin":"center axis of the second 4032a candidate; same internal interface as step253","root_transform_status":"internal pair registered; opposite-side transform is deferred because the view-turn icon does not encode a part transform"},"torso-rib-256-local":{"origin":"right-angle intersection datum of the two 3710 plates; fragment isolated at root X=2400","root_transform_status":"steps256–258 have a diagram-based local L layout; step255 corner subassembly remains unplaced, and neither inter-arm locking nor body transform is asserted"},"torso-detail-259-local":{"origin":"6541 hole-center datum; local +Z is the transverse hole axis and +Y is vertical","root_transform_status":"side 2736 candidate axis and span fit are registered; top brick/stud row is diagram-based; spacer stack withheld pending part identification"}},"joints":[{"id":"joint-skull-anterior-torso","type":"technic_pin_link_to_technic_mount","from":"completed_skull_rear_connector","to":"anterior_torso_technic_mount","evidence":{"manual_file":"6649862-2.pdf","printed_pages":[148,149],"steps":[278,279]},"connection_status":"instruction_confirmed","connector_parts_status":"geometry-compatible candidates placed: 32140 + 32184 + 2x11214; manual mold identification remains unconfirmed","relative_transform_status":"step_278_link_local_fit_applied; step247 single-port receiver aligned provisionally; step249 parallel-pair candidate fails a two-port axis test against the current +Y/+Z link ports; final pose and receiver variant unresolved","reason":"Step 278 shows two pins added to the black connector at the skull rear; step 279 calls out docking to the anterior torso. The local candidate connector is physically placed and its fit dimensions are recorded. Exact receiver parts and local attachment datums are not yet modeled, so the global transform cannot be derived from the overview alone. A provisional 6541 body-side receiver is placed against the third 32140 hole using official DAT hole center and axis; the callout-visible connection point and any intervening pin remain unconfirmed. Step249 candidate comparison used official LDraw hole axes and centers: current paired outlet axes are parallel, while the two candidate external link ports are orthogonal. Therefore do not claim simultaneous two-port engagement from the current arrangement.","connector_candidates":[{"part":"32140.dat","name":"Technic Beam 2 x 4 Liftarm Bent 90","status":"geometry_candidate_placed","geometry":"Two arm holes at 40-LDU pitch register to the 32184 axle stations; rendered silhouette matches the bent beam callout, but exact manual mold mapping remains unconfirmed."},{"part":"32184.dat","name":"Technic Cross Block 1 x 3 (Axle/Pin/Axle)","status":"geometry_candidate_placed","geometry":"Official axle bores register to the two 32140 holes at 40-LDU pitch; the orthogonal pin-hole remains available for the skull-side connection. Silhouette is consistent but not uniquely legible in the callout."},{"part":"98989.dat","name":"Technic Cross Block 2 x 4 (Axle/Pin/Pin/Twin Pin)","status":"rejected_by_hole_pattern","geometry":"Official 2x4 envelope and multi-hole pattern is larger than the compact two-station cross part shown; no matching two-hole pairing in the compared orientation."}],"alternative_connector_candidate":"98989.dat rejected for this two-station link by size and hole pattern; not retained as a current alternate.","pin_part":"11214.dat x2 geometry candidate; official geometry gives 20 LDU axle section into 32184, 20 LDU pin section within 32140, and 20 LDU exposed. Which endpoint is skull-side remains unresolved.","receiver_candidates":[{"part":"6541.dat","name":"Technic Brick 1 x 1 with Hole","status":"diagram_candidate_placed_tentatively","evidence":"Printed p136 step247 shows a single-hole black Technic brick above a two-piece vertical spacer stack. The official 6541 side-hole center/axis aligns with the third free 32140 bore; the two 6577s are vertical spacer candidates below it, not side-hole inserts. Exact bush mold and hidden lower support axle remain unverified."},{"part":"step249 paired 6541/3023 support","name":"two Technic single-hole blocks held between paired 1x2 plates","status":"local_two_port_candidate_with_axis_mismatch_to_current_link","evidence":"Printed p137 step249 inventory/callout shows two 6541s, plates, two short male-pin candidates and two round slotted joiners. The current official-DAT registration yields parallel +Z socket axes at 20-LDU pitch. The 278 link exposes candidate +Y and +Z ports; both cannot mate to this parallel pair simultaneously. An orthogonal variant or single-port engagement remains possible; the far-side callout does not settle it."}]}],"instances":[{"id":"part-0001","group":"stand","part":"4282.dat","gobricks_id":"517","sku":"GDS-517-031","color":19,"position":[0,0,0],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"candidate_unverified","placement_note":"Step 1 tan 2x16 base; datum center."},{"id":"part-0002","group":"stand","part":"36840.dat","gobricks_id":"1567","sku":"GDS-1567-072","color":72,"position":[-140,0,0],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"catalog_mapping_status":"candidate_unverified","placement_note":"Step 1 gray inverted bracket near one end; X approximate from diagram."},{"id":"part-0003","group":"stand","part":"3023b.dat","gobricks_id":"502","sku":"GDS-502-081","color":70,"position":[-100,-8,0],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"candidate_unverified","placement_note":"Step 2 first reddish-brown 1x2 plate; diagram placement."},{"id":"part-0004","group":"stand","part":"3023b.dat","gobricks_id":"502","sku":"GDS-502-081","color":70,"position":[-80,-8,0],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"candidate_unverified","placement_note":"Step 2 second reddish-brown 1x2 plate; stud locations provisional."},{"id":"part-0005","group":"stand","part":"54200.dat","gobricks_id":"833","sku":"GDS-833-081","color":70,"position":[-60,-8,0],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"candidate_unverified","placement_note":"Manual printed page 11 step 3; inventory visible, exact mold candidate and stud placement provisional."},{"id":"part-0006","group":"stand","part":"36840.dat","gobricks_id":"1567","sku":"GDS-1567-072","color":72,"position":[-20,0,0],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"catalog_mapping_status":"candidate_unverified","placement_note":"Manual printed page 11 step 3; inventory visible, exact mold candidate and stud placement provisi