"Only the two 6577 shape candidates are provisionally placed; the alternative 43093 pair is not instantiated, so candidates are not double-counted."},{"steps":"249","printed_page":137,"candidates":[{"feature":"6541 hole-axis relationship","status":"parallel_configuration_provisionally_placed; orthogonal_configuration_deferred","success_condition":"Parallel axes are retained only if both depicted 6541s and the through-view preserve the same-axis arrangement.","failure_condition":"A later underside/side view shows one 6541 rotated to expose a perpendicular receiver."}],"current_mpd":"One provisional parallel arrangement is recorded; the orthogonal alternative is not added as extra pieces. The user answered unclear/keep both; do not repeat the question."},{"steps":"252","printed_page":138,"candidates":[{"part":"50950.dat","quantity":1,"status":"provisional_shape_candidate","success_condition":"The long curved tan element has a 3x1 footprint and curvature matching the official 50950 shape; its base registers to the three preceding 11458 positions after the recorded turn.","failure_condition":"A later side/underside view shows a different curvature, stud/hollow pattern or attachment face."}],"current_mpd":"One provisional candidate instance is placed; it is not a confirmed mold ID or completed BOM quantity."},{"steps":"253–254","printed_page":138,"candidates":[{"part":"4032a.dat","quantity":2,"status":"strong_shape_candidate","success_condition":"The round element has four peripheral studs, a central open cross axlehole, shallow 8-LDU plate body without a raised collar, and two of its underside sockets align to the 3023b stud pair. This matches official 4032a.dat.","failure_condition":"A sharper underside/side view shows a center stud (18674), a 24-LDU brick with side pins (30000), a collared/circular bore or a different socket pattern."}],"current_mpd":"Two separate local pairs are represented because the instructions call for one pair in each step; 4032a mold identification remains provisional and these instances are excluded from confirmed quantity.","alternatives":[{"part":"18674.dat","evidence":"Official header is Plate 2x2 Round with 1 Centre Stud; the enlarged p138 callout shows a central open cross rather than a fifth/center stud.","status":"shape_mismatch_candidate_excluded_pending_better_view"},{"part":"30000.dat","evidence":"Official header is a full 2x2 brick with pins and axlehole; its 24-LDU brick-height/side pins conflict with the shallow round plate profile and two downward stud arrows.","status":"shape_and_height_mismatch_candidate_excluded_pending_better_view"}]},{"steps":"259","printed_page":140,"candidates":[{"part":"2736.dat","quantity":1,"status":"strong_function_shape_candidate","success_condition":"The round black element has a male axle stem concealed in the callout and enters the 6541 side crosshole; official 2736 DAT has a 17.5-LDU male shaft and towball head.","failure_condition":"A side view shows only a blind female axle socket with no male shaft, or ball size/stem orientation differs."},{"part":"32474.dat","quantity":1,"status":"function_mismatch_candidate_not_instantiated","success_condition":"Would require an unseen male axle pin inserted into its blind axlehole before the ball can attach.","failure_condition":"The shown element is directly pushed into the 6541 side opening; 32474 has no projecting male axle and cannot do that."},{"parts":["6577.dat","2780.dat"],"quantity":2,"status":"round_spacer_identity_deferred_not_instantiated","success_condition":"6577 if the callout shows female cross-axle bores; 2780 if it shows slotted male friction-pin stems.","failure_condition":"A sharper end view reveals the opposite sex/slot pattern."}],"current_mpd":"Only the 2736 towball candidate and callout brick/slope candidates are placed. Competing 32474 and spacer hypotheses are not instantiated."}]}}
